lisa-design:
- Repo set, kinds and dependency edges come from --manifest: sync --all = every release: true repo in Stages() order; the action's Dockerfile source = its single depends_on; ui sync dep and policies' OPA source = their go-service depends_on (OPA falls back to "agent").
- sync mode targets latest finals of every internal ref found (inside or outside the manifest, read-only for outside ones); train mode only the --set versions (+ OPA derived from the source repo's go.mod at its --set tag). --set versions must be semver; workflows refs only move when --workflows-ref/--set workflows is given.
- Without --pr ccf-bump only prints plan + diff; --pr --dry-run prints the PR it would open. Working copies are temp clones (GitHub, or --clones DIR for local dry runs); the user's clones are never modified.
- Branch ccf-bump/<mode>-<YYYY-MM-DD> is force-pushed and an open PR on it is updated, so a same-day rerun is idempotent. Older-date ccf-bump PRs are not closed (documented).
- Auto-merge only when no change is major (a new major, or a move from a pin that isn't a version / unknown current, e.g. real ui conformance or alpine -> mock-agent).
- One repo's failure is reported (::error::) and the rest still run; exit is non-zero.
- The token reaches git via GIT_CONFIG_* extraheader env (not argv/URL) and is stripped from the env of go and the repo's own sync script.
- ccf-bump-sync.yml: scheduled runs use repos.yaml and stay dry runs until repo variable CCF_BUMP_SYNC_LIVE == 'true' (so merging this doesn't start writing to product repos); dispatch has manifest + dry_run (default true). Token: read-only for dry runs; contents/pull-requests/workflows write when live (bumps edit workflow files). Commits authored as <app-slug>[bot].

lisa-selfreview:
pass 1 (strict, whole stack) — request_changes on this layer:
- CORE-INPUT-001: --set accepted non-version values; --all/--repos/--batch silently ignored with --repo; `sync --mode train` silently forced to sync.
- CORE-SEC (credential exposure): repo-owned sync script and go ran with GH_TOKEN in env.
- CORE-ERR: one repo's failure aborted the remaining repos of sync --all; `git diff` errors printed as "no file changes".
- docs: "every repo is scanned for every pin" inaccurate (kind-gated updaters).
pass 2 (strict) — approve. Deferred: superseded ccf-bump PRs from an earlier date are not auto-closed (documented; open question for reviewers).
